# Excludes from the Docker build context. Build context: projects/nocturne/.
# The Dockerfile re-installs + re-builds inside the image, so host install/build
# artifacts are excluded so a stale host .next / node_modules never shadows the
# in-image build. The Windows host .next/standalone is emitted with EPERM
# symlink warnings; excluding **/.next ensures the broken host trace can never
# leak — the Linux build stage produces a clean one. The apex/atrium precedent.

**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/dist
**/out
**/.cache
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/.eslintcache
**/playwright/.cache

# Local env files — secrets. nocturne needs NO runtime secrets (web-only); the
# only config is the build-time NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL ARG.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log

# Test + review surfaces — never executed at runtime.
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
e2e
**/playwright.config.ts
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/.lighthouseci
lighthouserc.json
web/lighthouserc.json
# Dev-time capture/verify scripts (their outputs are committed under docs/; the
# scripts do not run at runtime).
web/scripts

# Per-project docs — readable on GitHub, not needed in the runtime image.
**/README.md
**/CHANGELOG.md
**/PLAN.md
**/PROGRESS.md
**/DECISIONS.md
**/AGENT_NOTES.md
**/TASKS.md
**/CRITIQUE-*.md
**/REVIEW-*.md
**/DEPLOY.md
docs
web/docs

# The build/deploy descriptors themselves.
fly.toml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
